# Reference only. `intake setup` writes the real file into the profile's home,
# ~/.intake/syllabus/.env or ~/.intake/sous/.env (under $INTAKE_HOME if set),
# and never into the code directory. Each profile has its own.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional. The app creates a folder in My Drive on first upload ("Lecture
# Notes" for syllabus, "Client Calls" for sous) and files courses under it, so
# you normally leave these alone.
# DRIVE_ROOT_FOLDER_NAME=Lecture Notes
# DRIVE_PARENT_FOLDER_ID=

# Optional. Which microphone to record from, as a substring of the device name
# (see: intake record --list-devices). Names beat indices, which get
# reshuffled whenever a phone or headset connects.
# RECORD_DEVICE=MacBook Pro Microphone

# Optional. Send lecture action items to a Notion to-do database as dated
# tasks. Leave unset to skip Notion entirely. Create an integration at
# notion.so/my-integrations, then share your database with it (database ...
# menu, Connections), or every call returns 404.
# NOTION_TOKEN=ntn_...
# NOTION_DATABASE=https://www.notion.so/...

# "weekly" (default) puts a checkbox in the day column of your weekly page,
# which is the list you actually tick. "database" creates a row with
# Due/Course/Source fields instead. A row is invisible from the weekly page.
# NOTION_TARGET=weekly

# Optional. Only if `intake notion --check` maps a property wrong.
# Use the exact property name from your database.
# NOTION_PROP_DUE=Deadline
# NOTION_PROP_COURSE=Class
# NOTION_PROP_KIND=Type
# NOTION_PROP_SOURCE=Link

# Optional. Only when the panel is published through a Cloudflare Tunnel.
# The panel then asks anyone arriving that way to sign in with Google, and
# lets in only the addresses listed here. The client is a Web application
# OAuth client in the Google Cloud console, with
# https://<your hostname>/oauth2/callback as an authorized redirect URI.
# With all three set, a request that came through Cloudflare must carry a
# session from that sign-in. With any unset, every request that came through
# Cloudflare is refused. This Mac is never gated.
# PANEL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=0123456789-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
# PANEL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
# PANEL_ALLOWED_EMAILS=you@example.com, them@example.com
# The address the panel is published at. Google is sent back to
# <this>/oauth2/callback, so it must match what is registered on the client.
# Needed when the tunnel rewrites the Host header to the origin, as this
# one does; left empty, the request's own hostname is used.
# PANEL_PUBLIC_URL=https://syllabus.maincoursemedia.com
# Signs the session cookie. Leave unset and the panel generates one into .work.
# PANEL_SECRET_KEY=
